messages:
amanda: Quick note — ran into onboarding friction in the sample app where 403s are treated like auth errors and users keep retrying. Logs: `PermissionDenied` vs `AuthenticationError` confusion.
raj: ugh, saw that too in the Go SDK example. It raised AuthError for 403, but Python client raises PermissionDenied.
lena: Can you paste the snippet? curious if it's an upstream http status mapping issue or our wrapper.
amanda: pasted from the Node sample app earlier: ```js
try {
  await client.generate(...);
} catch (err) {
  // we currently do:
  if (err.status === 401 || err.status === 403) throw new AuthenticationError(err.message)
  throw err
}
```
raj: there — the blanket 401||403 -> AuthenticationError is the problem. 403 is often an authorization/permission thing where retrying won't help.
lena: agreed. For DX we should have typed errors that clearly indicate retry semantics: e.g. AuthenticationError (retry with backoff after reauth), AuthorizationError (no automatic retry), RateLimitError (retry after retry-after), ServerError (retryable).
dev-docs: +1 for explicit retry semantics in error docs. Also suggest we expose an isRetryable boolean on the error object so sample apps and customers can do the right thing without parsing status codes.
amanda: example mapping proposal: ```
// mapping table (status -> typed error, isRetryable)
401 -> AuthenticationError, true (reauth flow)
403 -> AuthorizationError, false
429 -> RateLimitError, true (respect Retry-After)
500-599 -> ServerError, true (exponential backoff)
400 -> BadRequestError, false
```
raj: can we keep names consistent across SDKs? Go currently uses NotAuthorizedError for 403 which doesn't convey the same meaning as AuthorizationError in Python.
lena: we should add a small shim layer in each SDK with canonical names and map language idioms to those names. e.g., Go: type AuthorizationError struct { ... } implement error; JS: class AuthorizationError extends RedwoodError.
amanda: also noticed sample-app onboarding docs recommend naive retry loops like `while (!ok) retry()` which will reauth but not surface to user why. We should update sample apps to show: check error.isRetryable and switch to interactive reauth or show clear message for 403.
dev-docs: I'll draft a short PR to the sample-apps repo with a single-file change demonstrating correct handling and comments. Will include a tiny table for mapping and the isRetryable pattern.
amanda: proposed sample snippet for apps: ```js
if (err instanceof AuthorizationError) {
  showToast('You do not have permission to perform this action. Contact admin.');
} else if (err.isRetryable) {
  await retryWithBackoff(() => client.call(...));
} else {
  throw err;
}
```
raj: sounds good. tiny nit — for 401 we should show reauth UI first before automatic retry so users know to sign in.
lena: action items: (1) dev-docs PR for sample apps + table, (2) SDK owners sync to align canonical error names and add isRetryable on error surface, (3) update onboarding docs to call out common gotchas.
amanda: I'll file the issues and tag SDK owners. Thanks! :thumbsup:
deploy-bot: deploy queued for docs branch update — status: pending checks.
dev-docs: FYI I'll include example unit test asserting each status maps to the canonical error type so parity is testable across SDKs.
raj: leaving a note for the Go SDK owner — @mike-oz we should avoid aliasing to NotAuthorizedError if it behaves differently.
lena: ok closing the loop here. small follow-up: add a log message in the sample app on 403 explaining next steps (contact admin), that alone should reduce support tickets.
amanda: perfect. I'll add the logs in the PR too.
